  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because \\quad \\delta_{\\mathrm{x}}^{2}=\\frac{\\Sigma \\mathrm{d}^{2} \\mathrm{i}}{\\mathrm{n}}$\r\nBut both $A$ and $B$ have 100 observations, then both the sample $A$ and $B$ have same standard deviation and the same variance.\r\nHence, $\\frac{\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{A}}}{\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{B}}}=1$",
